From aa76cad08ad7c224a32dcfaa712443b59642aa8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manoharan Sundaramoorthy <manoharan@nexthop.ai>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 14:04:59 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] zebra: keep NEXTHOP_FLAG_LINKDOWN in sync with carrier state

The kernel marks a route RTNH_F_LINKDOWN when its interface is admin-up but has no carrier. When carrier changes it sends only RTM_NEWLINK and does not re-send the route, so zebra kept a stale linkdown flag after carrier returned, and never set it when carrier was lost.

Set or clear NEXTHOP_FLAG_LINKDOWN in nexthop_active_check() for kernel and system routes from the interface state, and treat a change of the flag as a nexthop change so the route is reprocessed.

Include the flag in the nexthop group comparisons. nexthop_same() ignores flags, so without this a route is moved back to an existing nexthop group that differs only in LINKDOWN.

Add the zebra_linkdown_nhg topotest covering carrier loss and recovery.

Signed-off-by: Manoharan Sundaramoorthy <manoharan@nexthop.ai>
---
